I tend to play either a valkyrie or barbarian (I just like the swords
and kinky gear). As with everyone else, I sit in the first 5-6 levels
building up HP and levels (remembering to pray every so often) and
looking for shops. I don't hold too much with paying in shops so I use
several methods to rob them

a) pickaxe to prepare a pit just outside the shop... load up and run for
it
b) test any wands in the shop... wand of death/sleep/teleport are very
useful in shops. I find that shopkeepers resistance to magic is fairly
low and killing them is no hassle with a wand.
c) use that 'useless' potion of sickness/poison to weaken the 'keeper
and then paralysis to hold him and then beat him up. I have never yet
died trying this and find any of these tactics very profitable!
d) wand of teleport or scroll of teleport to get out. Forget the Kops.
As a level 5 or 6 barbarian or valkyrie they're really nothing to worry
about.

Chis

p.s. Who was it said that the Kops were tough guys... I usually find
them to be no problem and great for upping levels. Those cream pies can
be useful too.


